## MoveIt2 - Core Motion Planning Interface

The primary interface for motion planning and execution with MoveIt2.

### Constructor

```python
from pymoveit2 import MoveIt2

moveit2 = MoveIt2(
    node: Node,                                    # ROS2 node instance
    joint_names: List[str],                        # Robot joint names from URDF
    base_link_name: str,                           # Robot base link name
    end_effector_name: str,                        # End effector link name
    group_name: str = "arm",                       # Planning group name
    ignore_new_calls_while_executing: bool = False,# Block new goals during execution
    callback_group: Optional[CallbackGroup] = None,# ROS2 callback group
    use_move_group_action: bool = False,           # Use MoveGroup action vs ExecuteTrajectory
)
```

### Execution State Management

#### MoveIt2State Enum

```python
from pymoveit2 import MoveIt2State

class MoveIt2State(Enum):
    IDLE = 0       # No motion requested or executing
    REQUESTING = 1 # Execution requested, not yet accepted
    EXECUTING = 2  # Execution in progress
```

#### State Query Methods

```python
# Get current execution state
state = moveit2.query_state()  # Returns MoveIt2State

# Cancel current execution
moveit2.cancel_execution()

# Get future for async monitoring
future = moveit2.get_execution_future()  # Returns Optional[Future]

# Get last execution error code
error_code = moveit2.get_last_execution_error_code()  # Returns Optional[MoveItErrorCodes]
```

### Motion Planning & Execution

#### Move to Cartesian Pose

```python
moveit2.move_to_pose(
    # Pose specification (use ONE of these approaches):
    pose: Optional[Union[PoseStamped, Pose]] = None,     # Full pose object
    position: Optional[Union[Point, Tuple[float, float, float]]] = None,
    quat_xyzw: Optional[Union[Quaternion, Tuple[float, float, float, float]]] = None,
    
    # Frame and link options
    target_link: Optional[str] = None,         # Target link (default: end effector)
    frame_id: Optional[str] = None,            # Reference frame (default: base link)
    
    # Tolerances
    tolerance_position: float = 0.001,         # Position tolerance (meters)
    tolerance_orientation: float = 0.001,      # Orientation tolerance (radians)
    
    # Weights for multi-objective planning
    weight_position: float = 1.0,
    weight_orientation: float = 1.0,
    
    # Cartesian path planning options
    cartesian: bool = False,                   # Use Cartesian path planning
    cartesian_max_step: float = 0.0025,        # Max step size for Cartesian
    cartesian_fraction_threshold: float = 0.0, # Min fraction for success
)
```

#### Move to Joint Configuration

```python
moveit2.move_to_configuration(
    joint_positions: List[float],              # Target joint positions
    joint_names: Optional[List[str]] = None,   # Joint names (default: all joints)
    tolerance: float = 0.001,                  # Position tolerance (radians)
    weight: float = 1.0,                       # Planning weight
)
```

#### Plan Only (Without Execution)

```python
# Synchronous planning
trajectory = moveit2.plan(
    # Same pose/joint parameters as move_to_pose and move_to_configuration
    pose: Optional[Union[PoseStamped, Pose]] = None,
    position: Optional[Union[Point, Tuple[float, float, float]]] = None,
    quat_xyzw: Optional[Union[Quaternion, Tuple[float, float, float, float]]] = None,
    joint_positions: Optional[List[float]] = None,
    joint_names: Optional[List[str]] = None,
    frame_id: Optional[str] = None,
    target_link: Optional[str] = None,
    
    # Tolerances and weights
    tolerance_position: float = 0.001,
    tolerance_orientation: Union[float, Tuple[float, float, float]] = 0.001,
    tolerance_joint_position: float = 0.001,
    weight_position: float = 1.0,
    weight_orientation: float = 1.0,
    weight_joint_position: float = 1.0,
    
    # Starting state (default: current state)
    start_joint_state: Optional[Union[JointState, List[float]]] = None,
    
    # Cartesian options
    cartesian: bool = False,
    max_step: float = 0.0025,
    cartesian_fraction_threshold: float = 0.0,
) -> Optional[JointTrajectory]

# Asynchronous planning
future = moveit2.plan_async(...)  # Same parameters, returns Future

# Get trajectory from completed future
trajectory = moveit2.get_trajectory(
    future: Future,
    cartesian: bool = False,
    cartesian_fraction_threshold: float = 0.0,
) -> Optional[JointTrajectory]
```

#### Execute Pre-Planned Trajectory

```python
moveit2.execute(joint_trajectory: JointTrajectory)
```

#### Wait for Execution Completion

```python
success = moveit2.wait_until_executed()  # Returns bool
```

#### Reset Controller (Simulation)

```python
moveit2.reset_controller(
    joint_state: Union[JointState, List[float]],
    sync: bool = True,  # Wait for completion
)
```

